{{Otheruses|Children}}
{{Quote|Truly wonderful, the mind of a child is.|Jedi Grand Master Yoda|<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref>}}
[[File:GalacticPals-Younglings.png|thumb|300px|M1-RE with a group of younglings]]
"'''Youngling'''"<ref name="Dark Disciple">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref> or "'''cubling'''"<ref name="CEC">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> was a term for a child that was used by many [[species]].<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> [[Force-sensitive]] younglings who were taken to the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] to be [[Jedi training|trained]] as [[Jedi]] were known as "Jedi younglings"<ref name="Episode II" /> but had the specific title of "[[Jedi Initiate]]s."<ref name="DJL">''[[Dooku: Jedi Lost]]''</ref> Children in the [[Path of the Open Hand]] [[Religion|cult]] were known as the [[Littles]]. The title of "Children" was reserved for specific adults trusted by "[[Elecia Zeveron|the Mother]]" to carry out missions.<ref name="POD">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref>

[[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] once carried out a massacre on a group of Jedi younglings in the Jedi Temple on [[Coruscant]], as part of the [[Great Jedi Purge]].<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> Most young children needed adult supervision, as they could not take care of themselves on their own. When [[Din Djarin]] left the [[Din Grogu|Child]] aboard the ''[[Razor Crest]]'' all by himself, [[Peli Motto]] admonished the [[Mandalorian]], saying that he couldn't leave a child alone like that and that he had a lot to learn about raising a young one.<ref name="Gunslinger">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 5: The Gunslinger}}</ref> Bringing kids into gladiator matches was considered inappropriate; when Djarin brought Grogu to the [[Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk|Carnita arena]], a spectator pointed out that this was no place for a child, but the Mandalorian merely replied, "Wherever I go, he goes."<ref name="Marshal">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref>

As a child, [[Ben Solo]] coined a new name for himself but later dismissed it as "stupid." [[Snoke]] encouraged Solo to discard his old identity by taking the name that he invented during his childhood. He believed that children did not practice self-deception; therefore, they had only pure thoughts and were true to their nature.<ref name="Kylo 2">[[The Rise of Kylo Ren 2|''The Rise of Kylo Ren'' 2]]</ref>

During or after [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Pals Date">{{GalacticPalsDate}}</ref> several different species of younglings were stationed onboard the [[Youngling Care Space Station]]. The [[Safari droid]] [[M1-RE]], a specialized member of the [[Galactic Society of Creature Enthusiasts]], cared for and studied the younglings.<ref name="Learn to care">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-galactic-pals|text=Learn to Care for Creatures and Aliens in ''Star Wars Galactic Pals''}}</ref> The Safari droid [[SF-R3]] asked M1-RE to show viewers on the [[HoloNet]] how they could take care of their younglings, and M1-RE did so while being recorded by the [[cam droid]] [[CAM-E]].<ref name="Wookiee">{{GalacticPals|Loth-Cat}}</ref>

